Z||000007||Phil||03-02-2000||07:32 AM||||The wife packed two weeks worth of vacation clothes and stuff last year. We are getting to do the Power Tour again this year and I figure it will take 3 weeks to make the trip . It WILL fit.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||03-02-2000||08:37 AM||||My wife and I took our 85 GT from Tampa, Florida to Dallas, Texas and back in the late 80's. The wife had a business meeting and we stayed the week with a little side trip through New Orleans on the way back for some gumbo. As I recall, we stuffed the trunk and spare tire are with soft side luggage. We left enough room on top of the stuff in the trunk to place the garmet bag so nothing got wrinkled. We put a couple of bags of snacks in the passenger floorboard and still had plenty of leg room. Great trip!||||reg||10
Z||000009||wkayl||03-02-2000||09:10 AM||||I had myself, my 14 year daughter and all the stuff a 14 year girl packs for a 2 week stay at her grandparents.  I had to drive 800 miles this way!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000010||bHooper||03-02-2000||09:42 AM||||i once packed my GT to carry my then girlfriend and myself from north carolina to tampa/st pete for a week or so.  we had the trunk full (her stuff) the front full (my stuff) and even used the hooks behind the seats to hang more of her stuff!  plus we had  some things in the passenger floor board.<P>as for people, the most i've ever had were 2 extra's.  my buddy and his little brother who was like 11 or so, in the passenger seat.||||reg||1
